 library relies on several external libraries. We use the Armadillo C++ library [14] as our primary linear algebra engine. Armadillo is a C++ template library expression template techniques to optimize the performance of matrix expressions. Furthermore we utilize several Boost libraries [15]. Boost is a collection of free peer-reviewed C++ libraries; many of which are template libraries. For an introduction to these libraries see for example [16]. Use of multiple processors for cross validation and subsampling is supported through OpenMP [17]. sgl using","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":342.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":107.66666666666667,"r":502.3333333333333,"t":532.0},"charspan":[0,937],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"We provide two software solutions in relation to the current paper. An R package; nsgl, with relatively simple interface to our multinomial and logistic sparse group lasso regression routines. In addition; C++ template library; sg1, is provided. The template library gives access to the generic sparse group lasso routines. The R package relies on this library. The sg1 template library relies on several external libraries. We use the Armadillo C++ library [14] as our primary linear algebra engine. Armadillo is a C++ template library expression template techniques to optimize the performance of matrix expressions. Furthermore we utilize several Boost libraries [15]. Boost is a collection of free peer-reviewed C++ libraries; many of which are template libraries. For an introduction to these libraries see for example [16]. Use of multiple processors for cross validation and subsampling is supported through OpenMP [17]. sgl using"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The nsg1 R package is available from CRAN. The sg1 library is available upon request.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":313.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":109.33333333333333,"r":502.0,"t":344.3333333333333},"charspan":[0,85],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"The nsg1 R package is available from CRAN. The sg1 library is available upon request."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"5.1. Run-time performance","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":287.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":111.0,"r":253.33333333333334,"t":304.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,25],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"5.1. Run-time performance"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Table 3 lists run-times of the current multinomial sparse group lasso implementation for three real data examples. For comparison; the glmnet uses 5.2s, 8.3s and 137.0s, respectively; to fit the lasso for the three data sets in Table 3 The gImnet is a fast implementation of the coordinate descent algorithm for fitting generalized linear models with the lasso penalty or the elastic net penalty [10]. The gImnet cannot be used to fit models with group lasso or sparse group lasso penalty. path","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":184.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":109.0,"r":501.3333333333333,"t":286.0},"charspan":[0,494],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"Table 3 lists run-times of the current multinomial sparse group lasso implementation for three real data examples. For comparison; the glmnet uses 5.2s, 8.3s and 137.0s, respectively; to fit the lasso for the three data sets in Table 3 The gImnet is a fast implementation of the coordinate descent algorithm for fitting generalized linear models with the lasso penalty or the elastic net penalty [10]. The gImnet cannot be used to fit models with group lasso or sparse group lasso penalty. path"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"6 . Conclusion","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":154.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":110.66666666666667,"r":193.66666666666666,"t":167.0},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"6 . Conclusion"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"We developed an algorithm for solving the sparse group lasso optimization problem with a general convex loss function.  Furthermore; convergence","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":114.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":108.66666666666667,"r":501.3333333333333,"t":145.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,144],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"We developed an algorithm for solving the sparse group lasso optimization problem with a general convex loss function.  Furthermore; convergence"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"25","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":87.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":298.3333333333333,"r":312.3333333333333,"t":99.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"25"}],"version":"1.10.0"}